WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.839
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.139 --> 00:00:08.143
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.443 --> 00:00:13.812
Unit eight: City Life. In this unit, you will compare places and talk about life in the city.

4
00:00:14.817 --> 00:00:15.539
urban.

5
00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:18.552
urban means related to towns and cities.

6
00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:21.304
Urban areas are growing fast in Asia.

7
00:00:22.004 --> 00:00:24.007
Your turn. Say: urban.

8
00:00:26.707 --> 00:00:27.441
urban.

9
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:29.149
crowded.

10
00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:31.431
crowded means full of people.

11
00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:34.508
The market is very crowded on Sunday mornings.

12
00:00:35.208 --> 00:00:36.967
Your turn. Say: crowded.

13
00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:40.424
crowded.

14
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:42.278
skyline.

15
00:00:42.978 --> 00:00:45.837
skyline means the shape of buildings against the sky.

16
00:00:46.137 --> 00:00:49.274
Phnom Penh's skyline has changed a lot in ten years.

17
00:00:49.974 --> 00:00:52.267
Your turn. Say: skyline.

18
00:00:54.967 --> 00:00:55.782
skyline.

19
00:00:56.783 --> 00:00:57.738
nightlife.

20
00:00:58.438 --> 00:01:02.655
nightlife means entertainment and activities in the evening, like cafés and music.

21
00:01:02.955 --> 00:01:05.013
The riverside has a lively nightlife.

22
00:01:05.713 --> 00:01:08.121
Your turn. Say: nightlife.

23
00:01:10.821 --> 00:01:11.857
nightlife.

24
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:13.886
cost of living.

25
00:01:14.586 --> 00:01:18.931
cost of living means how much money you need for food, rent and other basic things.

26
00:01:19.231 --> 00:01:22.472
The cost of living in the capital is higher than in the provinces.

27
00:01:23.172 --> 00:01:26.045
Your turn. Say: cost of living.

28
00:01:28.745 --> 00:01:29.932
cost of living.

29
00:01:30.917 --> 00:01:32.092
public transport.

30
00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:36.243
public transport means buses and trains that everyone can use.

31
00:01:36.543 --> 00:01:39.053
Better public transport would reduce traffic.

32
00:01:39.753 --> 00:01:42.150
Your turn. Say: public transport.

33
00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.269
public transport.

34
00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:48.505
green space.

35
00:01:49.205 --> 00:01:52.412
green space means an area of grass and trees in a town.

36
00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:55.176
Cities need more green space for families.

37
00:01:55.876 --> 00:01:58.226
Your turn. Say: green space.

38
00:02:00.926 --> 00:02:02.253
green space.

39
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.042
suburb.

40
00:02:04.742 --> 00:02:07.926
suburb means an area where people live outside the city centre.

41
00:02:08.226 --> 00:02:10.434
We moved to a quiet suburb last year.

42
00:02:11.134 --> 00:02:13.369
Your turn. Say: suburb.

43
00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:16.942
suburb.

44
00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.903
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:20.203 --> 00:02:23.364
Do you prefer living in the city centre or in a suburb?

46
00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.581
The suburb. It's much quieter and a bit cheaper.

47
00:02:28.883 --> 00:02:31.324
But the city centre has far better nightlife!

48
00:02:32.617 --> 00:02:35.800
True, but it's far more crowded, and the cost of living is higher.

49
00:02:37.117 --> 00:02:40.893
I think the city needs more green space and better public transport.

50
00:02:42.183 --> 00:02:45.161
I agree. That would make urban life much easier.

51
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:49.831
Grammar focus: Comparatives: much · far · a bit.

52
00:02:50.131 --> 00:02:53.257
Use much or far before a comparative for a big difference.

53
00:02:53.557 --> 00:02:56.218
Use a bit or slightly for a small difference.

54
00:02:56.518 --> 00:03:00.793
For example: The suburb is much quieter, and this flat is a bit cheaper.

55
00:03:01.093 --> 00:03:04.985
Don't use 'very' with comparatives: say much bigger, not very bigger.

56
00:03:05.983 --> 00:03:08.926
Now read and listen. Phnom Penh Then and Now.

57
00:03:09.226 --> 00:03:12.247
Twenty years ago, Phnom Penh had very few tall buildings.

58
00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:17.384
Today, the skyline is far more modern, with dozens of towers.

59
00:03:18.683 --> 00:03:22.204
The city is also much more crowded, and traffic is a big problem.

60
00:03:23.517 --> 00:03:26.967
However, new parks have created more green space for families.

61
00:03:28.283 --> 00:03:33.011
Many residents hope that public transport will improve urban life even more.

62
00:03:34.317 --> 00:03:36.737
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:37.037 --> 00:03:40.569
An area outside the city centre where people live is a blank.

64
00:03:40.869 --> 00:03:44.348
A, skyline. B, suburb. C, nightlife.

65
00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:49.850
The answer is B: suburb.

66
00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.570
The city is blank busier than my village.

67
00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.513
A, very. B, much. C, more.

68
00:04:00.517 --> 00:04:02.458
The answer is B: much.

69
00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:06.344
This café is blank cheaper than that one.

70
00:04:06.644 --> 00:04:09.566
A, a bit. B, a lot of. C, many.

71
00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:15.097
The answer is A: a bit.

72
00:04:16.583 --> 00:04:19.465
How much money you need for basic things is the blank.

73
00:04:19.765 --> 00:04:23.802
A, cost of living. B, green space. C, public transport.

74
00:04:27.817 --> 00:04:29.944
The answer is A: cost of living.

75
00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:34.471
According to the text, what has created more green space?

76
00:04:34.771 --> 00:04:38.901
A, new parks. B, new towers. C, new roads.

77
00:04:42.917 --> 00:04:44.951
The answer is A: new parks.

78
00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:50.577
Now it's your turn to speak. Compare your town or city with another place you know.

79
00:04:55.877 --> 00:05:01.162
Phnom Penh is much busier than Kampot, but Kampot is far more relaxing and a bit cheaper.

80
00:05:01.462 --> 00:05:02.916
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:03.917 --> 00:05:08.926
Great work today! You learned eight new words and comparatives: much · far · a bit.

82
00:05:09.226 --> 00:05:12.459
Today's value is community. Help the people in your town.

83
00:05:12.759 --> 00:05:14.830
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

84
00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:18.154
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

